If the <normal equation> $A^TAc^*=A^Ty$ holds, the last two terms reduce to $\|Ah\|^2\geq0$, so $c^*$ minimizes. Conversely, at a minimizer the directional <derivative> in every $h$ vanishes, forcing $A^T(Ac^*-y)=0$.

