A set $A$ is $\mathcal C$-complete under many-one reductions when
$$
\boxed{A\in\mathcal C
\quad\text{and}\quad
(\forall B\in\mathcal C)\ B\leq_mA}.
$$
The first condition is membership in the class; the second is $\mathcal C$-hardness. This is a <many-one complete set>.

